{"action":"","actor":"","alternative_quotes":[],"choice_text":"","claimants":[],"concepts":[],"effective_periods":[],"jurisdiction":"","kind":"prohibition","logic_text":"(c) In checked baggage. A passenger may not transport or offer for transport in checked baggage or in baggage carried in an inaccessible cargo hold under § 1562.23 of this chapter:

(1) Any loaded firearm(s).

(2) Any unloaded firearm(s) unless—

(i) The passenger declares to the aircraft operator, either orally or in writing, before checking the baggage, that the passenger has a firearm in his or her bag and that it is unloaded;

